\DOC SUBSUMED_MAYCHANGE_TAC

\TYPE {SUBSUMED_MAYCHANGE_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Proves a goal of the form {t subsumed u}, where both sides are {MAYCHANGE}
state-relation expressions, closing it outright.

\DESCRIBE
The tactic takes no arguments. Applied to a goal whose conclusion is a
{subsumed} statement between two {MAYCHANGE} components (possibly {,,}-composed
and nested), it discharges the goal completely; the assumptions {A} are left
untouched and play no role in the outcome.
{
   A ?- t subsumed u
   ==================  SUBSUMED_MAYCHANGE_TAC
   (no goals)
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single behaviour — always a {subsumed}
conclusion between {MAYCHANGE} terms, with assumption lists ranging from a few
side conditions to large symbolic-execution states — and never any surviving
subgoal.

\ENDDOC
